  "boundaries": [
    "Original production source is byte-identical to base; five initial controls yield one pass/four expected failures, followed by one expected numeric ID failure. Test-only source and logs retained.",
    "Candidate-only wire-type and syntax-precedence regressions are separately preserved; they are not claimed as original-source findings.",
    "Only string, numeric and null IDs are echoed; raw ID serialization preserves token precision. Existing Axum feature already selected raw_value; no dependency version, lock or arbitrary_precision change.",
    "Argument admission precedes query/storage/worker acquisition. Notifications await owned execution and then return HTTP 204, preserving cancellation and snapshot checks.",
    "Nonempty JSON-RPC batch execution remains unsupported HTTP 422; empty batches are invalid requests. No new process-wide admission or response-memory bound.",
    "Detailed Ethereum filter semantics, retained WS snapshots, lag/reorg notifications, dashboard behavior, shared query resource policy and verified repair remain separate.",
    "No ingestion metadata writes, storage changes, SQL implementation, remote/production-data change, live sync or benchmark. No throughput claim."
  ],
